DESCRIPTION:----------\nObjective:\n----------\n\nProduce a research and en
 gineering poster that clearly communicates your final project.\n\nYou will
  be provided with a LaTeX poster template ([PDF] (https://drive.google.com
 /file/d/1SuTHaj9bLaWrai8mIYmK9wexUDZM7-3D/view?usp=sharing) and [TEX] (htt
 ps://drive.google.com/file/d/1nCGU43iB_8MtgABuRtDL8Uj6YAoeAN1u/view?usp=sh
 aring)) . The template is only a starting point and must be improved and c
 ustomized to suit your project.\n\nStudents must edit the LaTeX template\,
  compile it\, and submit the final poster as a PDF.\n\nFind the ALU Logo f
 ile [here] (https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UdWliNnNhaybZHMdraj1yFkpGrqAe
 vL5/view?usp=sharing)\n\n-------------\nInstructions:\n-------------\n\n1.
  Use the Provided Template\n----------------------------\n\nYou will use 
 the LaTeX poster template.\n\nStudents must:\n\n*\n\nUse the template as a
  starting point\n\n*\n\nImprove the design and layout\n\n*\n\nReplace all 
 placeholder content with their own work\n\n*\n\nAdd diagrams\, screenshots
 \, charts\, or architecture visuals\n\n*\n\nEnsure the poster clearly comm
 unicates the project\n\n* Compile the LaTeX file to generate the final pos
 ter\n\nThe template must not be submitted as-is. You are expected to adapt
  and improve it for your project.\n\n2. Poster Content\n-----------------
 \n\nYour poster should communicate the key aspects of your project. The te
 mplate includes sections such as:\n\n*\n\nProblem\, Context\, and Users\n\
 n*\n\nObjectives and Scope\n\n*\n\nProject Metadata\n\n*\n\nConstraints an
 d Design Decisions\n\n*\n\nProposed Solution and System Overview\n\n*\n\nM
 ethodology and Build Process\n\n*\n\nResults\, Evaluation\, and Demo Evide
 nce\n\n*\n\nImpact\, Contribution\, and Learning\n\n*\n\nLimitations and N
 ext Steps\n\n*\n\nReferences and Acknowledgements\n\nYou may adjust or ref
 ine these sections if needed to better present your project.\n\nFocus on:\
 n\n*\n\nclear explanations\n\n*\n\nstrong visuals\n\n*\n\nconcise text\n\n
 Avoid large blocks of text.\n\n3. Team Participation:\n-------------------
 ---\n\n* Ensure that all team members contribute to the poster presentatio
 n. Each member should be responsible for a specific part of the demo or ex
 planation (e.g.\, overview\, features\, technical overview\, system archit
 ecture\, technical challenges\, feedback).\n\n*\n\nPresentation format:\n\
 n*\n\n7–10 minutes presentation\n\n*\n\n3 minutes Q&A\n\n4. Prepare for 
 Q&A:\n-------------------\n\n* After the demo\, be prepared to answer ques
 tions. Focus on addressing questions related to the technical implementati
 on\, the impact on the project\, and the future potential of your solution
 .\n\n-----------\nSubmission:\n-----------\n\n* Submit the compiled poster
  PDF and any demo materials before the presentation.\n\n* Present live to 
 the class during the final session.\n\n*\n\nFile name format:\n\nTeamName_
 ProjectPoster.pdf\n\nSubmission rules:\n\n*\n\nOne submission per team\n\n
 *\n\nSubmit through Canvas\n\n*\n\nLate submissions follow the standard co
 urse late policy.
