DESCRIPTION:----------\nObjective:\n----------\n\nThis assignment documents
  the final outcome of your software project and demonstrates how the work 
 proposed earlier was implemented\, tested\, and evaluated. The report must
  present the completed system\, evidence of implementation\, system testin
 g\, results obtained\, and reflections on the development process. The goa
 l of this assignment is to show that your team successfully transformed th
 e proposed design into a working software solution.\n\nUse the official Fi
 nal Project Report [Template] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/15Or4rLv
 oDdwYZpPHu4i6IL19-CsZK6hM/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=106716268957962594436&rtpo
 f=true&sd=true) as your guide when writing the report. All sections and he
 adings provided in the template must be followed exactly.\n\n-------------
 \nInstructions:\n-------------\n\n------------\n1. Codebase:\n------------
 \n\n* Complete Codebase: Ensure your final project code is complete and we
 ll-organized.\n\n* GitHub Collaboration: Submit your code via GitHub\, ens
 uring all commits are documented and attributed to team members. The repos
 itory should demonstrate consistent collaboration using version control\, 
 including branches\, pull requests\, and issue tracking. Include a link to
  the GitHub repository in your final report.\n\n* Code Comments: Your code
  should be commented on\, explaining the purpose of key functions\, classe
 s\, and components to make the project understandable to other developers.
 \n\n-----------------\n2. Team Formation\n-----------------\n\n* Teams wi
 ll remain the same as those formed for the proposal assignment.\n\n* Provi
 de the same team name used in the proposal submission.\n\n* Assign clear r
 oles to each team member (e.g.\, Project Manager\, Lead Developer\, UI/UX 
 Designer\, Backend Developer\, Frontend Developer\, Database Architect\, T
 esting Engineer).\n\n* Ensure that each team member contributes to the imp
 lementation and development of the system.\n\n-------------------------\n3
 .Formatting Requirements\n-------------------------\n\n*\n\n*\n\nFont: Tim
 es New Roman\n\n*\n\nFont Size: 12 pt (main text)\, 14 pt (headings)\n\n*\
 n\nLine Spacing: 1.5\n\n*\n\nMargins: 1 inch on all sides\n\n*\n\nTable of
  Contents: Must be autogenerated\n\n*\n\nLists of Tables\, Figures\, and A
 cronyms: Must be included where applicable\n\n*\n\nCitation Style: APA for
 mat\n\n*\n\nPage Numbers: Required in footer\n\n*\n\nEach major section sh
 ould start on a new page\n\n--------------\n4. Submission:\n--------------
 \n\n* Submit all project documentation (PDF or Markdown files) alongside t
 he repository.\n\n* Include a link to the GitHub repository with access pe
 rmissions.\n\n* Demo video\n\n* Ensure all documentation is submitted befo
 re the deadline.\n\n* Team participation sheet.  Make a copy of the team 
 participation sheet [Link] (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1E_TU6Y
 zWaWctusfjszMGGZiEaLwjIUP3iyEIgMYaAXk/edit?usp=sharing) and edit the team 
 part and add your team name. Make sure that you add each team's role and p
 articipation. Also add team meeting and notes. Make sure that all sections
  and well completed before submission. Each assignment should have a uniqu
 e participation sheet.\n\nFinal Note: Any submission that does not include
  the team sheet will receive a score of zero. This is a group assignment\;
  however\, individual contributions will be closely monitored and assessed
  based on coding contributions only. README files\, documentation\, or oth
 er non-code materials will not be considered evidence of contribution. Usa
 ge of AI and AI code generative tools in ways not specified in this guidel
 ine will lead to serious penalties.
