X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span>Throughout your learning journey\, yo
 u have been working on developing </span><strong>mission statements</stron
 g><span> and exploring how your ideas can contribute to </span><strong>tra
 nsforming African communities</strong><span>.&nbsp\;</span><span>However\,
  a </span><strong>community is a puzzle\;</strong><span>&nbsp\;each missio
 n is one piece of that puzzle. When combined\, your missions can create a 
 more complete and sustainable vision for change.</span></p>\n<p><span>This
  assignment is designed to help you connect your individual missions\, col
 laborate as a team\, and practise </span><strong>storytelling as a tool fo
 r impact</strong><span>.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<h3><strong>Assignmen
 t Structure</strong></h3>\n<h4><strong>1. Intro Discussion (Mission Sharin
 g): The beginning of it all!&nbsp\;</strong></h4>\n<p><span>Each member wi
 ll share their </span><strong>mission statement</strong><span> with the gr
 oup.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><span>The goal of this stage is to </span><stro
 ng>listen\, understand\, and identify connections</strong><span> between y
 our different missions.</span><span><br><br></span></p>\n<p><strong>Guidin
 g questions&nbsp\;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>What eleme
 nts of your mission have you already started working on?</span><span><br><
 br></span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>What is the specific </span><str
 ong>community</strong><span> you are engaging with?</span><span><br><br></
 span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>What changes do you hope to achieve i
 n that community?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><i>Note: Remember to reco
 rd your conversation in the <span style="color: #e62429\;"><a class="inlin
 e_disabled" style="color: #e62429\;" href="https://docs.google.com/spreads
 heets/d/18VwVRsBEMcK0Pom9XZO_NPVsnZknHXHsfyDKVUTpOZ0/edit?usp=sharing" tar
 get="_blank">team task sheet.</a></span> Also\, prepare to work on your ne
 xt discussion. Book office hours with your learning coach\, and remember t
 his will count towards your final grade! </i></strong><strong><i><br><br><
 /i></strong></p>\n<h4><strong>2. Follow-Up Conversation (Collaboration &am
 p\; Integration)</strong></h4>\n<p><span>This part of the discussion shoul
 d help you think about </span><strong>partnership\, interdependence\, and 
 shared goals</strong><span>. Also\, remember that your goal is to ensure t
 hat there is growth in the community. The fact that your mission is a succ
 ess means that it contributes to the success of another mission. Remember 
 to consider that you are from different communities but still within Afric
 a. </span><span><br><br></span></p>\n<p><strong><i>Guiding questions: </i>
 </strong><span><br><br></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>What </
 span><strong>new lessons\, challenges\, or opportunities</strong><span> ha
 ve you discovered in your mission that could be valuable for the whole gro
 up?</span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>In what ways can </span><strong>
 these lessons help strengthen</strong><span> or expand the impact of the c
 ommunity you are serving?</span></li>\n<li aria-level="2"><span>If you wer
 e all working within the same community\, how could your </span><strong>mi
 ssions complement one another</strong><span>?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><stro
 ng><i>Note: Remember to record your conversation in the <span style="color
 : #e62429\;"><a class="inline_disabled" style="color: #e62429\;" href="htt
 ps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18VwVRsBEMcK0Pom9XZO_NPVsnZknHXHsfyDKV
 UTpOZ0/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank">team task sheet</a></span>. Also\
 , prepare to work on your next discussion. Book office hours with your lea
 rning coach\, and remember this will count towards your final grade!&nbsp\
 ;</i></strong></p>\n<p><span>&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<h4><strong>3. Closing Di
 scussion (Storytelling &amp\; Pitch)</strong></h4>\n<p><strong>Break the t
 alk into acts or segments that flow:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Act 1</stron
 g><span> – Setting the Stage (Speaker 1): One student introduces the sha
 red challenge or problem in a story-driven way. They pose the central ques
 tion\, like\, what if our communities could be self-sufficient?</span></p>
 \n<p><strong>Act 2 </strong><span>– Mission Stories (Speaker 2): The sec
 ond person shares their personal mission and story\, tying it back to the 
 bigger theme.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Act 3 </strong><span>– Integration 
 &amp\; Call-to-Action (Speaker 3): The final person shows how the missions
  connect and closes with a powerful vision for the future. It's a three-ac
 t talk\, but the challenge is for the students to deliver it as a unified 
 TEDx Talk by three storytellers and delivered as one story.</span></p>\n<p
 ><strong><i>Note: Remember to record your conversation in the team task sh
 eet. Also\, prepare to work on your next discussion. Book office hours wit
 h your learning coach\, and remember this will count towards your final gr
 ade!</i></strong></p>\n<p><strong><i></i></strong></p>\n<p><strong><i></i>
 </strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p><strong>Deliverables&nbsp\;</strong></p>
